    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Show that $f(x)=\\dfrac{2^{2x}+1}{2^x}$ is even.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(-x)=2^{-x}+2^x=f(x)$, so $f$ is even.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(-x)&=\\frac{2^{-2x}+1}{2^{-x}}\\\\&=2^{-x}+2^x\\\\&=\\frac{2^{2x}+1}{2^x}\\\\&=f(x).\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore $f$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
